{%- comment -%}
  The product page's lower accordions, from the theme's language files.

  Why here and not in the product's metafields: see the long comment in
  sections/walterin-buy.liquid where this is rendered. Short version — a
  metafield's Slovak lives outside the repo and has never once been written,
  and it cannot be previewed before it goes live.

  "As a gift" and "About Walter" are deliberately NOT product-specific: they
  say the same thing under every product, so they come from shared keys and one
  edit changes them everywhere.

  Accepts: product (required), prefix (required, e.g. "walterin.product.tarot_")
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign how_lead = prefix | append: 'how_lead' | t
  assign has_how = false
  unless how_lead contains 'Translation missing'
    assign has_how = true
  endunless
-%}

{%- if has_how -%}
  <details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
    <summary>
      <span class="wui-accordion__title">
        <span class="wui-label">{{ 'walterin.product.how_heading' | t }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
      <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">
        {%- comment -%}
          Two paragraphs, not three (Veronka, 9 Oct): the lead, which the stylesheet sets large,
          then everything else in one smaller paragraph. The two-readings text keeps its own key
          so it stays word for word what it was; it is only joined to the sentence before it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign how_text = prefix | append: 'how_text' | t
          assign how_readings = prefix | append: 'how_readings' | t
          assign how_body = how_text | append: ' ' | append: how_readings
        -%}
        <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: how_lead -%}</p>
        <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: how_body -%}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}

<details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
  <summary>
    <span class="wui-accordion__title">
      <span class="wui-label">{{ 'walterin.product.gift_heading' | t }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>
  <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
    <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">
      {%- comment -%}
        The lead is shared by every product. The text is not: "Pick the language they love to
        read in" is nonsense under the stickers, which have no language. So a product may carry
        its own <handle>_gift_text and it wins over the shared one. Nothing else forks — if a
        second product ever needs its own, it adds one key, not a new accordion.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign gift_text = prefix | append: 'gift_text' | t
        if gift_text contains 'Translation missing'
          assign gift_text = 'walterin.product.gift_text' | t
        endif
      -%}
      {%- assign v = 'walterin.product.gift_lead' | t -%}
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: v -%}</p>
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: gift_text -%}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
  <summary>
    <span class="wui-accordion__title">
      <span class="wui-label">{{ 'walterin.product.walter_heading' | t }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>
  <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
    <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">
      {%- assign v = 'walterin.product.walter_lead' | t -%}
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: v -%}</p>
      {%- assign v = 'walterin.product.walter_text' | t -%}
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: v -%}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
